{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1941","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Rudolf and 121"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Rudolf has an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers, the elements are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation, he can choose an index $$$i$$$ ($$$2 \\le i \\le n - 1$$$) and assign:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{i - 1} = a_{i - 1} - 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_i = a_i - 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_{i + 1} = a_{i + 1} - 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Rudolf can apply this operation any number of times. Any index $$$i$$$ can be used zero or more times."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can he make all the elements of the array equal to zero using this operation?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases in the test."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of elements in the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_j \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of the values of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is possible to make all the elements of the array zero using the described operations. Otherwise, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output each letter in any case (lowercase or uppercase). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be accepted as a positive answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n5\n1 3 5 5 2\n5\n2 4 4 5 1\n5\n0 1 3 3 1\n6\n5 6 0 2 3 0\n4\n1 2 7 2\n3\n7 1 0\n4\n1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\nNO\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the original array is $$$[1, 3, 5, 5, 2]$$$, to make all its elements zero, Rudolf can act as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" apply the operation at $$$i=4$$$ and get the array $$$[1, 3, 4, 3, 1]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" apply the operation at $$$i=3$$$ and get the array $$$[1, 2, 2, 2, 1]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" apply the operation at $$$i=2$$$ and get the array $$$[0, 0, 1, 2, 1]$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" apply the operation at $$$i=4$$$ and get the array $$$[0, 0, 0, 0, 0]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1941B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1941/problem/B"}